MIC = Message Integrity Code. It's a field inside the NTLM AUTHENTICATE message that signs the entire NTLM exchange (all three messages: NEGOTIATE, CHALLENGE, AUTHENTICATE). It's computed using the ExportedSessionKey. It's separate from SMB signing — MIC protects the NTLM messages themselves; SMB signing protects the SMB messages.



